# RIVAL Brand Voice & Copy

Full spec lives at `.cursor/brand-spec.md`. Apply these rules whenever writing or editing user-facing copy.

## Primary tagline
**Step out of the stands.** — hero brand line, use everywhere.

## Other taglines (context-specific)
- Mission / about: **From spectator to rival.**
- Conversion / social / ads: **Rival everyone.**
- Community / The RIVAL Elite: **The fans who play.**
- First match / onboarding: **This is your game now.**
- Live / in-app moments: **No dead time.**
- Influencer / creator: **The game the match creates.**

## Website hero formula (per spec §07)
> Step out of the stands.
> "RIVAL is the live multiplayer game played inside every match. Create chaos. Rival everyone in your lobby."
> CTA: **Join The RIVAL Elite.**

## Brand voice
- **Direct** — no preamble, no filler. Every word earns its place.
- **Alive** — present tense, active voice. Copy happens now, not past tense.
- **Competitive** — carry the energy of someone who wants to win, but always welcoming.
- **Collective** — "we" over "you". RIVAL is a movement.
- **Confident** — no hedging, no "kind of". RIVAL knows what it is.
- **Never corporate** — no "gamified", "second screen", "engagement", or "interactive experience".

## Words to use
| Use | Instead of |
|---|---|
| Rivals | users / players |
| The RIVAL Elite | early adopters |
| The lobby | game session |
| The match | the game (that's RIVAL) |
| Season | period / phase |
| Chaos | (owned — use deliberately) |

## Words to avoid
`gamified` · `second screen` · `passive viewing` · `users` · `predict` (sounds like betting) · `platform` · `engagement` · `interactive experience` · `never a dull game` · `don't watch, play` (anti-watching framing)

## What RIVAL is and isn't
- **Not a betting app** → a live multiplayer game. No gambling language. No money changes hands.
- **Not a quiz app** → a competitive live game. Questions are the mechanic; rivalry is the product.
- **Not fantasy sport** → the game inside the live match. Live, minute-to-minute.
- **Not anti-watching** → pro-immersion. RIVAL makes watching better. Never position as a replacement.

## Early adopter / The RIVAL Elite framing
> "The fans who got here first are building what RIVAL becomes."

Season 1 players are pioneers, not beta testers. Use The RIVAL Elite language in all early-access and waitlist copy.
